Dame Quay is a [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] Pactbroker and Argyle's contact within the organization. She answers his calls at a private line and keeps the file on his work, and she has offered to send an information packet to his residence when there is anything to report.

She is folded out of paper, greyish-yellow, her face and arms unfolding and folding again as she flips through a folder. She works from a guarded office and does not wear a raiment. She answers to a supervisor of her own, who is busy.

She is blunt and hard to satisfy. She calls Argyle dangerous, however friendly he and his new group seem, and thinks he has gotten himself into something. She would rather not send him straight back out. Anything bearing his number that reaches her, she takes as coming from him, and her records include a fax he sent from a Pactbroker station in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]].

She is asking members of the [[Org/The Scale/index|Everchain]] whether they have seen the like of the two [[Ugathal]] that ambushed Argyle's group in Hallia. She has briefed Argyle in a smoke-filled room with the goat-legged fiend he calls [[Divinity/Fiends/Flintlock Toboggan|Flintlock]] present, who wears suit trousers cut below the knee and a vest over burn-scarred skin. She has already misappropriated a national relic for him, and says she will not do it a second time. She can send a few people beyond the fracture, though the slow way takes about six months and leaves them out of action in the meantime.

From her reading of the Party's progress along the crossing, she reckons they are about halfway to [[Geography/The Quorum|the Quorum]], the place where the [[Org/The Scale/Voice of Many|Voice of Many]] was found, which is still firmly the territory of [[Divinity/Fiends/Sigzil Haight|the Shackled Prince]], and she warns that it holds good items but is a place her own people did not long hold. Asked to look into the founding member of the Scale, the party that went with him, and the strider they crossed on, she says she will ask around, though she doubts much of it is public.
